{
  "_about": "The A1 word list the Italian course is measured against (Dan, 2026-11-14): every entry marked A1 in the Italian Kelly list, headwords only. It stands in for the Profilo della lingua italiana A1 inventory, which is published only on the book's CD-ROM. An entry that names several forms (il, lo, la; un, uno, una) is split into its forms, so 1013 entries give 966 words. Kelly grades by corpus frequency, most frequent first, so this list leans to written web Italian more than a syllabus list would. Core target (Dan, 2026-11-14): the 600 most frequent of these words, in Kelly rank order, as French uses FLELex's 600 most frequent; the full list is the stretch goal.",
  "source": "Kelly project (Keywords for Language Learning for Young and adults alike), Italian list it_m3.xls, https://ssharoff.github.io/kelly/",
  "license": "CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/)",
  "citation": "Kilgarriff, A., Charalabopoulou, F., Gavrilidou, M., Johannessen, J. B., Khalil, S., Johansson Kokkinakis, S., Lew, R., Sharoff, S., Vadlapudi, R. and Volodina, E. (2014). Corpus-based vocabulary lists for language learners for nine languages. Language Resources and Evaluation 48, 121-163.",
